    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n37748" root="لطأ" body-key="l">
    
      1 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">لَطَأَ بِالأَرْضِ</span></b> , aor. 
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">لَطَاَ</span></b> , inf. n. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">لَطْءٌ</span>; and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">لَطِئَ</span>,
aor. 
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">لَطَاَ</span></b> , inf. n. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">لُطُوْءٌ</span>; <i>He clave to the ground.</i>
(S, K.) Also, the former, without <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ء</span>: <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">إِلْطَهْ</span> occurs in a trad. for <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">إِلْطَأْ</span> [imper. of <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">لَطِئَ</span>] <i>Cleave to
the ground.</i> (TA.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">لَطِئَ لِسَانِى</span> <i>My tongue
became stiff, so that I could not move it to speak.</i>
From a trad. (TA.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">لَطَأَ</span>, (K,) inf. n. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">لَطْءٌ</span>,
(TA,) <i>He beat</i> a person with a staff or stick:
or <i>he beat on the back</i> only. (K.)

